  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 239 AM MST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nStarting on Friday, ensemble models are in agreement that\nupper-level southwesterly flow will likely occur over the Tri-\nState area. On Saturday morning and throughout all of Sunday, a\nsmall trough and ridge wave could slide through over from the\nsouthwest and bring in a weak cold front before sliding out of\nthe area to the northeast. Once this feature passes, is it\nexpected that southwesterly flow would likely return on Monday.\nWith this being said, chances for precipitation looks to be\nnon-existent with cloud coverage being scattered before building\nback up Monday. Winds are forecast to be breezy on Friday with\nspeeds between 20 and 30 mph with possible gusts over 35 mph\nfrom the southwest before calming back down to 10 to 15 mph for\nthe remainder of the period. \n\nWhile temperatures on Friday are forecast to be above seasonal\naverage, it is expected for temperatures to be back to normal \nafter the cold front passes over Saturday morning. As afternoon \nhighs are expected be in the 40s, morning lows are forecast to \nbe in the 20s and warm slightly back up into the 30s on Monday \nmorning.",
